# The mutual-action comparison and long-root contradiction

The original chosen G₂(4) geometry and the swapped symplectic marking yield
an elementary inner actor of rank four whose whole moved space has binary
dimension four. The exports retain the literal weak-closure conjugate,
commutator, normalizer action and induced image. Small movement places the
actor in a literal conjugate highest-root group of rank two, completing the
rank contradiction. Constructing the swapped module and paired flags remains
with the enclosing triangle assembly.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith, 11.4.1(2), printed p.776.
-/
